**Bug:** `src/import_merge.ts:7` compared incoming and existing URLs with strict string equality (`b.url === inc.url`), which is case-sensitive. Since hostnames are case-insensitive, `https://example.com/a` and `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` weren't recognized as the same entry.

**Fix:** Added a `sameUrl` helper (lines 3-18) that normalizes both URLs via `URL` and compares `href` — which lowercases the host while preserving path and scheme. Malformed URLs fall back to case-insensitive string comparison.

Verified against the bug report plus edge cases (different host/path/scheme stay distinct; identical URLs merge with unioned tags). Lint clean.


